From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:32:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: mt6359-auxadc: Include the ADC resolution in the
 scale

The scale omitted the ADC resolution: on the MT6358 BATADC channel, raw
code 25383 was reported with a scale of 5400 instead of 5400/32768 mV
per count, and generic-adc-battery's conversion of the result
overflowed. Divide by 2^realbits, and reject a channel descriptor with
a zero ratio denominator instead of dividing by it.

On the Zinwa Q25 the scale becomes 0.164794921 and the battery reads
4.182 V.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c b/drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c
index f426a289..b365b19f 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c
@@ -769,14 +769,14 @@ static int mt6359_auxadc_read_raw(struct iio_dev *indio_dev,
 	int ret;
 
 	if (mask == IIO_CHAN_INFO_SCALE) {
-		*val = desc->r_ratio.numerator * cinfo->vref_mV;
+		if (!desc->r_ratio.denominator)
+			return -EINVAL;
 
-		if (desc->r_ratio.denominator > 1) {
-			*val2 = desc->r_ratio.denominator;
-			return IIO_VAL_FRACTIONAL;
-		}
+		*val = desc->r_ratio.numerator * cinfo->vref_mV;
 
-		return IIO_VAL_INT;
+		/* RAW is an ADC code; include its resolution in the scale. */
+		*val2 = desc->r_ratio.denominator << chan->scan_type.realbits;
+		return IIO_VAL_FRACTIONAL;
 	}
 
 	scoped_guard(mutex, &adc_dev->lock) {
